# Player Authentication Flow (register → sign-in → me)
# Requires the backend running locally (Development profile, port 5041).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5041
@contentType = application/json
@accept = application/json

### 1. Register a new player
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/player/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}

{
  "login": "alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Secret123"
}

### 2. Register with a duplicate login → 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/player/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}

{
  "login": "alice",
  "email": "other@example.com",
  "password": "Secret123"
}

### 3. Register with a duplicate email → 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/player/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}

{
  "login": "bob",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Secret123"
}

### 4. Sign in with LOGIN → 200 + JWT
# Use the "token" value from the response for the "me" request.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/player/sign-in
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}

{
  "identifier": "alice",
  "password": "Secret123"
}

### 5. Sign in with EMAIL → 200 + JWT
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/player/sign-in
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}

{
  "identifier": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Secret123"
}

### 6. Sign in with a wrong password → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/player/sign-in
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}

{
  "identifier": "alice",
  "password": "WrongPass1"
}

### 7. Sign in with an unknown user → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/player/sign-in
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Accept: {{accept}}

{
  "identifier": "ghost",
  "password": "Secret123"
}

### 8. Get current player with a valid Bearer token → 200
# Paste the token from step 4 below.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/player/me
Authorization: Bearer <PASTE_TOKEN_HERE>
Accept: {{accept}}

### 9. Get current player WITHOUT a token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/player/me
Accept: {{accept}}